Option Meaning <code>numba</code> whether compilation takes place. Omit to compile if numba is installed, else run uncompiled. <code>True</code> demands compilation (raises <code>ImportError</code> if missing). <code>False</code> runs uncompiled even if numba is installed. <code>parallel</code> enable parallel compilation (see per-decorator semantics) <code>fastmath</code> enable Numba's <code>fastmath</code> (faster, less precise floating point) <code>cache</code> forward Numba's on-disk cache, skipping compilation in later processes <p>Any other option (<code>boundscheck</code>, <code>nogil</code>, <code>inline</code>, …) can only be passed to the decorator; the model channel accepts exactly these four keys.</p> <pre><code>@cm.template
class MyModel:
    @cm.precompile(parallel=True)
    def mutate(self, K: "Array[float, 2]"): ...


model = MyModel(seed=1, parallel=True, cache=True)   # all kernels it owns
</code></pre>
